# thoughtBench Roadmap

This roadmap describes major capability milestones. Dates are intentionally omitted — this project optimizes for correctness, usability, and power over speed.

---

## MVP-1 (Foundation) ✅
**Status:** Complete

- Native SwiftUI app (macOS + iPadOS)
- SQLite-backed persistence
  - Conversations
  - Messages
  - Attachments metadata
- File import surface (foundation)
- Chat UI scaffolding
- Console-style layout groundwork
- Local-first storage philosophy established

---

## MVP-2 (Core LLM Workbench) 🚧
**Status:** In progress  
**This is the first *usable* release**

- Local LLM engine integration
- Model manager
  - Persistent model locations
  - External drives supported
  - Multiple roots allowed
- Per-message controls
  - Edit prompt (row-specific)
  - Try again (same context)
  - Response grading
- Chat history persistence
- Model selection per conversation
- Keep-alive + session reuse
- Zero-terminal usage required

---

## MVP-3 (File Intelligence)
- Native file parsing
  - PDF
  - DOCX
  - XLSX / XLSM
  - Images
- Preview + reference inside chat
- Attachment-aware prompting
- Retrieval groundwork (non-embedding-first)

---

## MVP-4 (Workspaces)
- Dedicated workspaces
  - Swift
  - Python
  - HTML/JS
- Console views per workspace
- Export snippets
- Iterative comparison tools

---

## MVP-5 (Power User + Automation)
- Prompt templates
- Response scoring analytics
- Workflow macros
- Local agents
- Optional cloud sync (explicit opt-in)

---

## Long-term
- Plugin system
- Model benchmarking
- Team/local-network sharing
- Enterprise/private model support